  "narrative": "The independent validation for H8 weakens the candidate association between feature_027 and outcome_006. The discovery estimate was +0.030 with a 95% interval of -0.014 to +0.074, and the approximate absolute 10% clinical threshold for outcome_006 is about 0.0175. The validation estimate is much smaller, +0.0096, with a very wide independent interval of -0.054 to +0.074. The validation therefore does not reproduce a clinically meaningful claimed-direction effect and does not justify acceptance. It is not possible to reject H8 categorically because the validation interval still includes clinically meaningful positive values, but the original positive result now appears more likely to be a borderline or false discovery than a supported finding. I deprioritize the original H8 comparison while retaining feature_027 in related follow-up screens across other outcomes. I also registered two outcome_006 interaction refinements to test whether the failed validation reflects effect heterogeneity within major balanced strata rather than absence of signal. These remain dataset-specific discovery associations; opaque predictor labels do not support causal or biological interpretation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 1 synthesis: no accepted claims. H8 validation failed to reproduce the discovery effect: R13 estimate 0.0096, independent interval -0.0543 to +0.0736, below the approximate clinical threshold 0.0175. H8 status remains unresolved but is deferred as the original comparison. Active/registered follow-up includes feature_027 main effects on outcome_013, outcome_014, outcome_011, and outcome_008, feature_050 main effects on outcome_003, outcome_004, outcome_009, and outcome_010, plus newly proposed feature_027 interactions with feature_034 and feature_002 for outcome_006. H7, H11, and H12 remain deferred and underpowered. H1-H5, H9, and H10 remain closed rejects. Do not claim causality or generalizability; all conclusions are limited to the supplied dataset."
